{"name":"Mecha Grey","hex":"#8d847f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mecha","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large armoured robot on legs, typically controlled by a pilot seated inside."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mecha"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mecha","blocks":[{"text":"In science fiction, mecha  or mechs are giant robots or machines, either depicted as piloted or sentient and are typically humanoid walking vehicles. The term was first used in Japanese after shortening the English loanword 'mechanism'  or 'mechanical' , but the meaning in Japanese is more inclusive, meaning any mechanism in general, and 'robot'  or 'giant robot' is the narrower term referring to robots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/%E3%82%AF%E3%83%A9%E3%82%BF%E3%82%B9%E3%83%BBMaker_Faire_Tokyo_2012_%281%29.jpg/330px-%E3%82%AF%E3%83%A9%E3%82%BF%E3%82%B9%E3%83%BBMaker_Faire_Tokyo_2012_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mecha","wikidata":"Q858784"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com